From: Animesh Kumar <animesh.kcm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] transcription: log cache read/write failures instead of silently swallowing

The transcription cache helpers catch every Exception and continue. That
preserves pipeline availability but loses the failure cause. Switch to
logger.exception so the root cause appears in logs without changing the
control flow.

Reported in improvements/code-review.md#cr-01.

---
 src/agents/transcription.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/agents/transcription.py b/src/agents/transcription.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/agents/transcription.py
+++ b/src/agents/transcription.py
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ def _check_cache(audio_hash: str, engine) -> TranscriptionResult | None:
             return None
         finally:
             session.close()
-    except Exception:
+    except Exception:  # cache miss must not break the pipeline
+        logger.exception("Transcription cache read failed")
         return None

@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ def _save_cache(audio_hash: str, result: TranscriptionResult, engine) -> None:
             session.commit()
         finally:
             session.close()
-    except Exception:
-        pass  # Cache save failure is non-critical
+    except Exception:
+        logger.exception("Transcription cache write failed (non-critical)")
